    {
      "challengedBy": [],
      "claim": "When `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` and `CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_ENDPOINT` are set, `refreshOAuthTokens` returns the raw `fetch()` Response (`return response;`) rather than the parsed JSON/token payload that callers consume. Callers such as `packages/app-store/googlecalendar/lib/CalendarService.ts` and `packages/app-store/zohocrm/lib/CalendarService.ts` pass that return value into `parseRefreshTokenResponse(...)` or read token fields from it, so the code path will fail to expose `access_token`/`refresh_token` and can throw `Invalid refreshed tokens were returned` or break field reads at runtime.",
